          "en": "on whether the users sign up or in at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 22.56,
          "en": "That's also something we'll take care about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 24.9,
          "en": "But first of all, let's make sure we can send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "to the login endpoint as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 29.67,
          "en": "For that, in the auth service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.67,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "let's start by adding a new login method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 37.11,
          "en": "and login also takes a email and also takes a password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.11,
          "end": 40.233,
          "en": "which should also be a string unsurprisingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.76,
          "end": 45.21,
          "en": "And in login we still have to send a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.21,
          "end": 47.46,
          "en": "Let's check out which URL we should send it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.46,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "to here in the Firebase auth REST API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 53.22,
          "en": "If we wanna sign in, this is the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.22,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "the URL we should send the request to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 58.26,
          "en": "It should be a POST request, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 60.57,
          "en": "In the other let's, in the login method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "in the auth service, use the Angular HTTP client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 67.35,
          "en": "and send a POST request to that URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.35,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "Now again, that API key needs to be replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 72.93,
          "en": "and therefore obviously we use the same API key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.93,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "as up there for signing up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 77.28,
          "en": "Let's grab that and replace it down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.28,
          "end": 81,
          "en": "including the square brackets just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "And this login request also takes a email, a password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 90.28999999999999,
          "en": "and this returnSecureToken key as a request body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 93,
          "en": "And that of course is the exact same body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 94.41,
          "en": "as we have here for signing up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.41,
          "end": 97.02000000000001,
          "en": "So I can just copy and paste it from there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.02000000000001,
          "end": 98.07300000000001,
          "en": "just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.24000000000001,
          "end": 101.55,
          "en": "This will now send such a HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.55,
          "end": 103.89,
          "en": "Let's see which data we get back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.89,
          "end": 107.55,
          "en": "For that in the officially docs, we see we get almost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 111.78,
          "en": "the same response as we got it for signing up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 114.81,
          "en": "But there is one extra field, the registered field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 117.99000000000001,
          "en": "which is a Boolean, and therefore to be able to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.99000000000001,
          "end": 120.84,
          "en": "that same authResponseData interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 123.93,
          "en": "I'll add registered here, but add a question mark to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.93,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "indicate that this is optional and a Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "because the signup request will actually not yield it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 132.933,
          "en": "but the log request will yield it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.07,
          "end": 137.79,
          "en": "So now here on logging in, I will also add the angled",
          "zh": ""
        },
